estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "A provenance projection exists on activity, events and history that emits author, author_source, agent_harness, agent_instance and every declared agent_provenance dimension without any JSON Patch payload, and its per-row cost stays within a small constant of the compact projection rather than a multiple of it; The row surfaces accept predicates on the recorded provenance dimensions, at minimum harness, model, effort and agent_instance, using the same filter grammar the existing --author and --op filters use, and an unknown dimension name fails fast naming the declared set rather than returning zero rows; Selecting one concurrent agent is possible: two processes of the same harness writing in the same window are separable by agent_instance through a documented filter, proven by a test that runs two writers and asserts each predicate returns only its own entries; A corpus-level coverage answer is cheap: a bounded summary reports how many entries carry each provenance dimension and how many do not, without transporting the entries, so an operator can measure provenance completeness before trusting any grouping; Dimensions added later flow through automatically: adding a declared dimension to the descriptor contract makes it projectable and filterable with no edit to activity, events, or history, proven by a fixture dimension that no built-in harness declares; The projection and the predicates are public SDK primitives first and the CLI flags are thin callers of them, so a package or an external consumer can build fleet analytics without reimplementing history parsing"
